WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.850
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
on Game of Thrones we got some more callbacks

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:11.670
to the Iron Bank of Braavos, Syrio Forel’s
unknown status and Sansa in the Vale.

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:13.970
But really I feel like all the energy was
at Crasters.

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:17.660
Quick heads up to, if you’re finding me
for the first time I do weekly Game of Thrones

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:19.710
videos with all kinds of bonus stuff.

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:21.340
This week is round 5 of my giveaway.

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:28.849
All you have to do is participate is be a
subscriber and leave a comment.

00:00:28.849 --> 00:00:31.360
Because I’m getting ready to hit 200,000
subscribers just as a way to say thank you

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:32.360
I’m doubling it.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:33.360
So I’m picking two random people from the
comments to give giftcards to.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.360
So let’s talk about love triangles and the
moon door.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:36.370
Careful for spoilers from the episode if you
haven’t seen it yet.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:40.200
Here are my top 5 WTF moments, Number 5 - Lysa
and Littlefinger

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:44.770
In case you don’t remember from Season 1,
she is looney tunes crazy.

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:46.130
Mostly crazy for Littlefinger.

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:50.450
It’s kind of tragic how much he’s taken
advantage of her lifelong obsession with him.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:54.750
But here are the cliff’s notes on their
historic love triangle with Catyln Stark.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:59.789
Littlefinger loved Catlyn as a boy, but she
like most teenagers wasn’t always crazy

00:00:59.789 --> 00:01:00.789
for him.

00:01:00.789 --> 00:01:04.739
Her younger sister Lysa became obsessed with
him.

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:08.549
Because Littlefinger couldn’t have Catelyn,
he took Lysa as consolation prize.

00:01:08.549 --> 00:01:10.810
He basically took her virginity.

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:12.880
Only making her obsession worse.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:17.660
But she was forced to marry the much much
much older John Arryn who ruled The Eyrie.

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:23.600
John Arryn discovered Joffrey was a bastard
but Littlefinger who was working a long con

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:28.790
at the time, used Lysa’s obession to get
her to poison her husband slowly and send

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:32.439
that letter to Catelyn that made her think
the Lannisters were responsible.

00:01:32.439 --> 00:01:39.960
Which is part of the reason Catelyn took Tyrion
to the Vale to be executed in season 1.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:50.610
That was only the half of things in the Vale
in the episode, we can unpack the freaking

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:53.299
hilarious sex screaming in the comments.

00:01:53.299 --> 00:01:57.810
But the big takeaway from Sansa this week
is that Lysa looks like she could flip out

00:01:57.810 --> 00:01:59.560
and try to do something awful to her.

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:00.909
Keep you eyes peeled on Lysa.

00:02:00.909 --> 00:02:03.009
Robin Arryn, her son.

00:02:03.009 --> 00:02:04.601
Is like a crazy Joffrey analog.

00:02:04.601 --> 00:02:08.520
He’s just crazy at the opposite end of the
spectrum.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:13.129
Who else felt awful for Sansa when he just
farted out his mouth about the Red Wedding?

00:02:13.129 --> 00:02:15.730
Number 4 - You Can’t Run From The Iron Bank

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:20.610
This may not have seemed like a big deal,
but I think this Iron Bank plot will become

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:22.730
a much bigger thing in a few episodes.

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:27.280
But how surprised were you when Tywin Lannister
said all their gold mines had been exhausted.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:30.610
They’re still rich, but there’s no new
money coming in.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:34.150
All those wars that he funded and the money
he lent to Robert also took a huge chunk of

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:35.150
their wealth.

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:37.290
So that’s why they need the Tyrells.

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:41.110
They’re the only other super wealthy family
in Westeros right now.

00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:46.050
Mark Gatiss is playing someone from the Iron
Bank, but no word on which episode he’ll

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:47.050
debut in.

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:52.849
It actually seemed like there were a lot of
big call outs to Braavos in the episode.

00:02:52.849 --> 00:02:55.500
Number 3 - Daenerys Does What Queens Do

00:02:55.500 --> 00:03:00.530
I liked the casual way Daario talked about
taking Meereen’s fleet of ships.

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:05.000
It’s basically enough to carry the force
they have right now to Westeros.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:09.239
So technically if they wanted to, they could
probably take the Iron Throne and enough people

00:03:09.239 --> 00:03:12.670
would just flock to her banner to help them
subdue the rest of Westeros.

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:15.730
They wanted it to feel like Daenerys could
go either way.

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:19.890
But in doing so, all of her good work freeing
slaves would be undone.

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:24.129
So she’s sticking around.

00:03:24.129 --> 00:03:27.319
But her enemies are starting to come back.

00:03:27.319 --> 00:03:30.790
They name dropped Cleon, a former Slave who’s
taken over Astapor.

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:36.459
He’s going to be important so remember him.

00:03:36.459 --> 00:03:39.300
Back in Yunkai the Wise Masters took power
back.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:42.360
So they’re also going to be a group Daenerys
will have to face again.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:50.299
We didn’t see the dragons, but I expect
we’ll see them again soon.

00:03:50.299 --> 00:03:54.720
Number 2 - Brienne and Podrick world’s best
Odd Couple, next to Brienne and Jaime

00:03:54.720 --> 00:04:01.129
Yes, it’s a bummer that Jaime is there with
her, but I love the comedy they brought to

00:04:01.129 --> 00:04:02.159
the episode.

00:04:02.159 --> 00:04:06.620
When the whole world is burning or freezing
around you it’s nice to get some relief.

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:11.299
She’s slowly warming up to him but it was
really when she learned about how Pod saved

00:04:11.299 --> 00:04:14.569
Tyrion from the Kingsgaurd at Blackwater that
sealed the deal.

00:04:14.569 --> 00:04:19.900
I feel like this also foreshadowed Pod saving
Brienne at some point this season.

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:24.180
He’s not super at cooking rabbits but he’s
there when you really need him.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:28.250
I also loved the way they visually connected
Pod talking about running his spear through

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:32.090
the back of the kingsguard’s skull and the
way Jon Snow killed Karl.

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:35.840
and my number 1 WTF moment, no surprise here
- Jon Versus Karl

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:39.700
We’re going to miss you Burn Gorman, you
were an amazing villain.

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:44.470
In case you were wondering, he died inside
Craster’s Keep and because they lit it on

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:45.970
fire, I think he burned too.

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:47.910
So he won’t come back as a Wight.

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:49.900
The fight scene was pretty amazing too.

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:53.680
There is a lot of swordplay or water dancing
in Arya’s case.

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:58.060
But we don’t get really pitched intimate
battles like this very often.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:01.660
I thought David and Dan did a really good
job of developing Karl as a villain so that

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:05.310
this final fight felt like such a high point.

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:06.480
That shot of Jon’s sword though.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:10.720
That will go down as one of the all time best
killing blows on the show.

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:14.669
Not quite as big as Ned Stark’s beheading,
but definitely Top 5.

00:05:14.669 --> 00:05:17.710
Now it’s your turn, let me know what your
favorite moment was.

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:21.590
Jon and Karl, Arya and the Hound or Sansa
in the Eyrie?

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:27.370
Because there were so many big things going
on, here’s some notes on things we also

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:29.380
have to pay attention to:

00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:34.380
Arya is water dancing again and she let the
hound know he’s on her list of people to

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:35.380
kill.

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:37.889
I was so happy that Needle couldn’t penetrate
his armor.

00:05:37.889 --> 00:05:41.669
I love the two of them as a pair.

00:05:41.669 --> 00:05:44.169
They’re like the anti Pod and Brienne.

00:05:44.169 --> 00:05:47.820
Or Pod and Brienne are like the anti Arya
and the Hound.

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:54.419
Let’s just call them Team Fuck the King.

00:05:54.419 --> 00:05:58.280
The Hound also had a big wink to the fandom
about Syrio Forel.

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:02.740
Everyone always wants to know whether he’s
dead or not, and the Hound thought that Meryn

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:10.280
Trant couldn’t kill himself with his own
blade if he tried.

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:13.880
So if you believe him, that means Syrio is
still alive.

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:17.310
In reality, George RR Martin never said what
his fate was in the books.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:23.570
And in every interview I’ve ever seen he
refuses to say for certain what happened to

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:24.570
Syrio.

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:27.600
So let me know whether you think he really
died or not.

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:31.960
Then let’s follow up with Bran, it looks
like he’s back on track to find that giant

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:33.530
weirdwood from their visions.

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:38.509
Poor Hodor too, did you see the look on his
face when he realized he killed Locke.

00:06:38.509 --> 00:06:42.830
And then there was the major Sand Snakes namedrop.

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:44.480
Oberyn talked about his 8 daughters.

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:49.070
I know a lot of you have been asking me if
we’ll see any of them this season.

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:53.240
Based on the pacing of the episodes and given
the fact we’re halfway done with the season,

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:57.099
I don’t think the show will bring them on
until Season 5 at the earliest.

00:06:57.099 --> 00:07:03.539
If there’s anything important that you thought
I didn’t mention, just write it in the comments.

00:07:03.539 --> 00:07:05.389
Overall the episode was a solid A minus.

00:07:05.389 --> 00:07:08.160
They did an amazing job of paying off the
Karl plot, which was developed beautifully

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:11.020
even though he wasn’t even in that many
scenes.

00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:13.240
I think Burn Gorman really nailed evil.

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:15.310
I hope he plays some more villains in the
future.

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:19.240
He looked like he had so much fun.

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:22.560
The way they revealed the Vale and the Eryie
was also really breathtaking.

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:27.480
You go from the Bloody Gates, this horrible
claustrophobic Kill Box to that big panoramic

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:34.370
CG shot of the castle at the top of the mountain.

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:39.210
The idea is that Sansa is supposed to be safe
from armies there, but because of crazy pants

00:07:39.210 --> 00:07:44.262
Lysa and Robin, she’s probably in just as
much danger as she was in King’s Landing.

00:07:44.262 --> 00:07:49.879
Emotionally the Bran breakaway at the end
didn’t land with me, mostly because I know

00:07:49.879 --> 00:07:55.389
the book canon and Bran never went to Caster’s
in the books, so the whole subplot was a little

00:07:55.389 --> 00:07:57.180
surreal to me.

00:07:57.180 --> 00:08:01.000
But Jon’s reunion with Summer was so good.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:06.960
It probably touched me so much because I’m
a dog person, I’ve had big Labrador Retrievers

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:07.960
my whole life.

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:10.490
So I know what it’s like to love a big animal
like Summer.

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:15.190
I didn’t expect them to try and top the
White Walker scene from last week.

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:17.949
But Karl’s death came pretty close.

00:08:17.949 --> 00:08:23.879
I felt like the whole Meera thing was building
towards them dying a horrible death, so it

00:08:23.879 --> 00:08:32.190
wasn’t a huge surprise that Jon stabbed
him in the back of the skull.

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:33.190
Podrick Style.

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:35.419
Let me know if you have any other lasting
questions about the plot or what’s coming.

00:08:35.419 --> 00:08:36.419
Next week based on the teaser Tyrion’s Trial
starts.

00:08:36.419 --> 00:08:37.419
So I’m really excited to watch that play
out.

00:08:37.419 --> 00:08:38.419
My Q&amp;A will post tomorrow.

00:08:38.419 --> 00:08:42.180
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:50.100
One more time, thank you so much you guys
for helping me get to 200,000 subscribers.

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:54.790
You’re all awesome.

00:08:54.790 --> 00:08:58.410
Right now click here for that Q&amp;A, i’ll
add the annotation as soon as i post it.

